      "preprocess.xml upsamples the 864x496 source to the TARGET 2560x1536 canvas before VAE encode (same",
      "architectural fact as the 1920x1088 config, re-confirmed by spatial-resolution-independence of the",
      "model architecture) -- so all three submodels run at the 2560x1536-derived latent grid (320x192 ==",
      "2560/8 x 1536/8), not at the 864x496 input's native resolution.",
      "PER EXPLICIT REQUEST: the VAE decoder here is modeled UNTILED (full-frame, exactly like the VAE",
      "encoder's own convention) -- NO 2x2 spatial tile grid is applied, unlike the 1920x1088 config's",
      "real-pipeline K=4-tile behavior. Decoder conv/groupnorm/fc/attention h/w below are the FULL per-tier",
      "frame dimensions (same tier-derivation pattern as the encoder: full/2/4/8), and calls use the BASE",
      "(1 INIT + 29 ACTIVE = 30 temporal segments only) counts with NO x4 tile multiplier -- i.e. exactly",
      "the same calls values the 1920x1088 config used BEFORE its 2x2-tile correction was discovered.",
      "Resolution tiers (full -> /2 -> /4 -> /8-latent), matching the 1920x1088 config's tier-derivation",
      "pattern exactly: full=1536x2560, tier/2=768x1280, tier/4=384x640, tier/8(latent)=192x320.",
      "DiT video_tokens recomputed for the new latent grid: video_tokens = T_latent * H_latent * W_latent / 4",
      "(same /4 patchify factor empirically confirmed for the 1920x1088 config via SEEDVR2_DIT_BOUNDARY",
      "shape=[252960,2560] matching 31*136*240/4 exactly) = 31 * 192 * 320 / 4 = 476160 (vs 252960 before).",
      "hidden_size/qkv_size/intermediate_size/num_heads/head_dim/num_layers/txt_tokens are architectural",
      "constants, UNCHANGED by resolution.",
      "DiT windowed-attention num_windows: NOT independently re-derived from a real log at this resolution",
      "(no such log exists yet) -- APPROXIMATED by scaling the 1920x1088 config's num_windows proportionally",
      "with the video_tokens ratio (476160/252960 = 1.8822), assuming a roughly fixed per-window token count",
      "(the standard windowed-attention design point): wattn_window_a 100->188, wattn_window_b 150->282.",
      "Flagged as an approximation, not a measured/derived fact like the rest of this file.",
      "GroupNorm is ov::op::internal::GroupNormalizationZSplit (SeedVR2-specific), same as the 1920x1088",
      "config. VAE ENCODER convs are kind=plain (no CausalConv3DCarry in its exported IR, same architectural",
      "fact, resolution-independent); VAE DECODER convs are kind=causal (33 CausalConv3DCarry nodes in its",
      "exported IR, same architectural fact) with the op's own carry_in port supplying temporal history --",
      "t_body/kind/kernel/stride values copied VERBATIM from the 1920x1088 config (temporal structure is",
      "resolution-independent), only h/w (and DiT's token-derived m/s) were recomputed for this resolution.",
      "1x1x1 shortcut/upscale convs and kernel_t==1 spatial-only downsamplers are always plain Convolution",
      "in both submodels (no temporal context needed) -- same as before.",
      "All shapes here are UNVALIDATED against any real OV_VERBOSE log at this resolution (none exists) --",
      "this is a first-principles resolution re-derivation from the ALREADY-VALIDATED 1920x1088 config,",
